STILL DISCLOSED, not defects in this build:
  - WHICH METRIC THE SLOT WAS RESERVED FOR IS MISSING, and was not guessed.
  -    The code comment, the CSS comment and the commit that introduced the
  -    card all describe it as reserved without saying what for. The ticket
  -    records the one measured candidate -- the per-tract adjustment figures
  -    are the only Con Edison overlay pair the panel never renders -- as an
  -    observation about the data, not as a statement of intent.
  - A SECOND "Coming soon" REMAINS IN THE BUNDLE, in Section D, and is
  -    deliberately untouched: it is assigned to a variable that is never
  -    interpolated, so it reaches no operator. It is dead code rather than a
  -    placeholder anybody sees, and removing it is its own change.
  - THE MAP COULD NOT BE PAINTED IN THE BUILD ENVIRONMENT, so the rendered
  -    check is the owner hosted pass. Leaflet and Turf load from unpkg.com
  -    and the build sandbox has no network, so the map never initialises
  -    there and renderMapKPI never runs. The panel was instead produced by
  -    the shipped function against the real map payload and painted under
  -    the real stylesheet, which is where the measurements above come from.
  - THE HTML DOES NOT CHANGE in this wave beyond its cache-busting stamps,
  -    and the byte comparison against the live copy is what decides what is
  -    pushed, not this note.

